] [17592186544811 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544811 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following conditional probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2y}{2x+3} & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,x+1\\le y\\le x+2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(Y<2\\,|\\,X=\\frac{3}{4}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544811 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "427792fe-a52b-5a35-ba4b-43ed95fe05d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544811 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that \n\n$$\nP(Y\\in A\\,|\\,X=x)={\\int }_{A}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ is the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x.$ \n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y<2\\,|\\,X=\\frac{3}{4}) & ={\\int }_{1+x}^{2}{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x=\\frac{3}{4})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1+3/4}^{2}\\frac{2y}{(2\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}+3)}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}{\\int }_{7/4}^{2}2y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}[{y}^{2}]_{7/4}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}(4-\\frac{49}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544823 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186544667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544823 #edb/ref 1069 "q-145091" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544823 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544823 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{8}({y}^{2}+x), & \\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ for $0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544823 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5ffa5cf0-3e04-5a20-bfc9-964d09fea30a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544823 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the formula for the marginal density function for $Y,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3}{8}({y}^{2}+x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{3x}{8})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3x{y}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{16}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6{y}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{12}{16}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}({y}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}({y}^{2}+1), & \\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow recall that the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal density function for $Y.$\n\nNow, for $1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3}{8}({y}^{2}+x))}{(\\frac{3}{4}({y}^{2}+1))} \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}+x}{2({y}^{2}+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}+x}{2({y}^{2}+1)}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544888 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186544738 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544888 #edb/ref 1069 "q-143644" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544888 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544888 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}6, & \\,y\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y},\\,0<y<1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ for $y\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y},\\,0<y<1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544888 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e1e5b64b-413b-5b25-a4f6-89eb28f41500" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544888 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the formula for the marginal density function for $Y,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{y}^{\\sqrt{y}}6\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\cdot x\\,{|}_{y}^{\\sqrt{y}} \\\\  & =6(\\sqrt{y}-y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}6(\\sqrt{y}-y), & \\,0<y<1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow recall that the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal density function for $Y.$\n\nNow, for $y\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y},\\,0<y<1,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{6(\\sqrt{y}-y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}-y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}-y}, & \\,y\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y},\\,0<y<1, \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544915 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186544930 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544915 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "30248955-d920-5775-b526-08ed5f2dc18c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544915 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186162392 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544930 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186544949 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544930 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5d882eb4-16fb-59da-b62d-8a906e410df4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544930 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186544811 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544931 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186544915 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544931 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "62bdfc51-9355-5143-887f-ba5e070d3107" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544931 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186162391 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544944 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7a34afb8-c474-5763-b3ff-41b909b64888" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544944 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186544823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544949 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186544944 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544949 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8674c106-cb3c-5923-8462-3b9e2322b1df" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544949 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186544888 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
